docs/idea-summaries/images/05/parent-selection-at-birth.svg
     1	<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1320 640" width="1320" height="640" font-family="Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" role="img" aria-labelledby="t d">
     2	<title id="t">What each parent-selection rule knows about two new nodes</title>
     3	<desc id="d">Hypothesis. One parent has two new children, one with degraded code (orange) and one with structured code (blue), each with one evaluation and the same outcome. Each row pairs a rule with what it outputs for both nodes: DGM sees one development score, HGM sees the same counts and gives one shared density, and HGM with a structural prior adds code features and gives the two nodes different densities. Densities share one clade-success scale and are illustrative.</desc>
     4	<defs><marker id="m64748b" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#64748b"/></marker></defs>
