docs/idea-summaries/images/05/refactor-first-break-even.svg
     1	<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1260 560" width="1260" height="560" font-family="Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" role="img" aria-labelledby="t d">
     2	<title id="t">When refactoring first pays off</title>
     3	<desc id="d">Illustrative accept-if-better model. Search alone removes error at per-evaluation rate r0. Refactoring first spends a fixed cost in evaluation-equivalents with no gain, then removes error at a higher rate r1 (0.015 against 0.010). The curves cross at the break-even budget B*, about three times the refactor cost.</desc>
     4	<defs></defs>
     5	<rect x="0.75" y="0.75" width="1258.5" height="558.5" rx="16" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e5e7eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
     6	<text x="40.0" y="50.0" font-size="20.1" font-weight="700" fill="#1f2328" text-anchor="start">Refactoring first can pay off past a break-even budget</text>
     7	<line x1="130.0" y1="450.0" x2="1010.0" y2="450.0" stroke="#4b5563" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
