docs/idea-summaries/images/05/two-tier-design.svg
     1	<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1360 700" width="1360" height="700" font-family="Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" role="img" aria-labelledby="t d">
     2	<title id="t">Two tiers: many cheap edits, fewer loops</title>
     3	<desc id="d">Top: the eight-cell resolution IV half fraction over modularity, observability, parameters and checks (I = MOPT), crossed with 20 base harnesses and three proposers; cells 1 and 8 also get naming and control arms. Bottom: three of the 20 bases give 96 configurations (32 settings each, naming opaque or physical). Each gets a profile forecast and a clade estimate at matched cost, and each predictor is correlated within base with the sealed-test gain of ten validation loops.</desc>
     4	<defs><marker id="m64748b" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#64748b"/></marker></defs>
     5	<rect x="0.75" y="0.75" width="1358.5" height="698.5" rx="16" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e5e7eb" stroke-width="1.5"/>
     6	<text x="40.0" y="50.0" font-size="20.1" font-weight="700" fill="#1f2328" text-anchor="start">Tier 1 measures profiles cheaply; tier 2 checks them against full loops</text>
     7	<text x="40.0" y="100.0" font-size="18.9" font-weight="700" fill="#1f2328" text-anchor="start">Tier 1: single-edit profiles</text>
     8	<text x="40.0" y="128.0" font-size="16.5" font-weight="400" fill="#4b5563" text-anchor="start">Eight-cell half fraction (I = MOPT) x 20 bases x 3 proposers</text>
     9	<rect x="243.0" y="150.0" width="54.0" height="204.0" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
    10	<rect x="705.0" y="150.0" width="54.0" height="204.0" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
