docs/idea-summaries/images/05/refactor-first-break-even.svg:2:<title id="t">When refactoring first pays off</title>
docs/idea-summaries/images/05/refactor-first-break-even.svg:3:<desc id="d">Illustrative accept-if-better model. Search alone removes error at per-evaluation rate r0. Refactoring first spends a fixed cost in evaluation-equivalents with no gain, then removes error at a higher rate r1 (0.015 against 0.010). The curves cross at the break-even budget B*, about three times the refactor cost.</desc>
docs/idea-summaries/images/05/refactor-first-break-even.svg:6:Refactoring first can pay off past a break-even budget
