docs/idea-summaries/images/05/parent-selection-at-birth.svg:2:<title id="t">What each parent-selection rule knows about two new nodes</title>
docs/idea-summaries/images/05/parent-selection-at-birth.svg:3:<desc id="d">Hypothesis. One parent has two new children, one with degraded code (orange) and one with structured code (blue), each with one evaluation and the same outcome. Each row pairs a rule with what it outputs for both nodes: DGM sees one development score, HGM sees the same counts and gives one shared density, and HGM with a structural prior adds code features and gives the two nodes different densities. Densities share one clade-success scale and are illustrative.</desc>
docs/idea-summaries/images/05/parent-selection-at-birth.svg:6:Hypothesis: code features separate new nodes that score and count alike
