docs/idea-summaries/images/05/same-outputs-different-futures.svg:2:<title id="t">Same outputs, different futures</title>
docs/idea-summaries/images/05/same-outputs-different-futures.svg:3:<desc id="d">Two harnesses, A and S, produce identical scores on every input. A is a single long function, S is split into typed, logged stages. Under the same optimizer and budget, their illustrative improvement curves start from the same point and diverge; the hypothesized gap comes from how the code is written.</desc>
