codex
**needs-attention**

Do not launch the full study. The revision fixes the missing-score denominator and removes sealed participants from adaptive gates. It also defines a within-base forecast and restores HGM’s own-node evidence at cold start. The revised design can still declare frontier equivalence while real effects cancel, validate a refactor crossover on people who helped select the refactor, and produce an undefined forecast for the hardest configurations.

1. **High — H6 uses its validation participants to accept refactors.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:223) · `line_start` 223 · `line_end` 226 · confidence 0.98  
   The gated arms accept edits using execution on selection participants, then use those same participants to measure the crossover. Hiding labels still lets their inputs influence which code survives. The prediction also profiles only the first seed’s refactor, while the other seeds can produce different code. **Recommendation.** Gate on development and synthetic inputs, freeze the checkpoint incumbents, and validate on independent participants. Either reuse one frozen refactor across search seeds or profile each refactor whose crossover is measured.

2. **High — H2 can declare equivalence when individual effects are large.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:219) · `line_start` 219 · `line_end` 221 · confidence 0.99  
   In the `I=MOPT` half fraction, O and M×P×T are identical columns. Opposing effects can cancel, so all four frontier TOSTs can pass without establishing equivalence for the individual factors. More edits in the same eight cells increase precision around the aliased contrasts. **Recommendation.** Add the complementary eight cells for the frontier proposer and power the resulting marginal contrasts, or limit the equivalence claim to the aliased contrasts.

3. **High — H3’s forecast is undefined when no edit succeeds and is tested against a different search policy.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:125) · `line_start` 125 · `line_end` 150 · confidence 0.99  
   Smoothing the success rate leaves mean gain undefined when zero of 300 edits succeed. Dropping those configurations would preferentially remove the hardest cases. The formula describes a single-incumbent search, while H3’s primary target averages five such loops with five OpenEvolve archive loops. **Recommendation.** Predefine a finite estimate for zero-success profiles, such as the mean gain across all proposals with zero assigned to failures. Test it first against single-incumbent loops and report archive transfer separately.

4. **High — The equivalence gate can break the paired experiment.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:176) · `line_start` 176 · `line_end` 184 · confidence 0.97  
   The protocol discards individual cells that fail the gate. If a structured transform fails on a difficult base while its degraded counterpart passes, the primary contrast can compare different sets of bases. The sealed audit also has no stated consequence if a surviving variant disagrees with its base. **Recommendation.** Require complete matched cell sets for each primary contrast, and preregister how a sealed mismatch invalidates the affected contrast before outcome scores are opened.

5. **High — H5 still leaves the biomechanics clade counts undefined.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:158) · `line_start` 158 · `line_end` 166 · confidence 0.97  
   The proposal defines success for a whole edit, then pools per-task successes without specifying the comparison parent, guard scope, or what the root contributes. A descendant can improve over its immediate parent on a task while remaining worse than the clade root. Those two implementations can rank the same archive differently. HGM’s own-node update is restored, and Figure 6 is now illustrative. **Recommendation.** Freeze one per-task event and define its reference, missing-score and guard rules, and root handling. Apply the same counts to both priors and the H3 baseline. [HGM expansion policy](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.21614#S3.SS3)

6. **Medium — The coding replication’s CPU budget lacks a defensible estimate.** [Proposal](/Users/theodoremui/dev/bioharness/docs/idea-summaries/05-what-makes-a-harness-improvable.md:298) · `line_start` 298 · `line_end` 304 · confidence 0.95  
   The table calls CPU cost “small” for 125,000 profile task attempts plus at least 16,000 replication task evaluations. In the cited Polyglot protocol, HGM and DGM used 347 and 2,385 allocated CPU-hours respectively per 800 evaluations. At those rates, five seeds of those two arms alone would use about 13,660 CPU-hours. The proposed setup can differ, but it supplies no measured replacement rate. **Recommendation.** Benchmark an end-to-end Polyglot run and itemize task execution, proposer expansion, reruns, and final scoring before committing the budget. [HGM Polyglot results](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.21614#S4.SS2)
tokens used
